 ],
 "literal": "She indeed, your word having taken, my word having trusted, / under the shelter of many branches of the fresh-budded ñāḻal tree, / having lost her fresh beauty, she has great loneliness. / Look over there! You must think of her. / Like moonlight and darkness, with fishy-smelling waves, / the ocean and the seaside grove appear, / in our small, good village with drooping-leaved palmyra palms.",
 "translation": "Believing my words, which were based on your promises, she now stands under the shelter of the many-branched, fresh-budded ñāḻal tree, having lost her fresh beauty and filled with deep loneliness. Look over there! You must think of her. In our small, beautiful village where palmyra palms with drooping leaves stand, the ocean and the seaside grove appear together, like moonlight and darkness side by side.",
 "modern": "உன்னுடைய வார்த்தைகளை நம்பி நான் சொன்ன சொற்களை ஏற்றுக்கொண்ட இவள், பசுமையான அரும்புகளைக் கொண்ட ஞாழல் மரத்தின் பல கிளைகளின் நிழலில் ஒதுங்கி நின்று, தன் புதிய அழகை இழந்து தனிமையால் வருந்துகிறாள். அதோ பார்! நீ அவளைப் பற்றி நினைக்க வேண்டும். மடல் தாழ்ந்த பனை மரங்களைக் கொண்ட எங்களது சிறிய நல்ல ஊரில், நிலவும் இருளும் போலப் புலால் நாற்றமுடைய அலைகளைக் கொண்ட கடலும் கடற்கரைச் சோலையும் ஒன்றாகத் தோன்றுகின்றன.",
 "explanation": "The playmate (தோழி) speaks to the hero (தலைவன்) who has been delaying his marriage, urging him to marry the heroine (தலைவி) soon. She points out how the heroine, having trusted the hero's promises conveyed through her, now stands in deep grief and loneliness under a blooming ñāḻal tree. The playmate directs his attention to their small coastal village, where the dark seaside grove (கானல்) and the bright sandy shore or ocean (கடல்) appear side by side like darkness and moonlight. This striking visual contrast of light and shadow reflects the heroine's inner conflict and her transition from the brightness of love to the darkness of despair. By highlighting her fading beauty and the vivid landscape of their village, the playmate reminds the hero of his duty to protect and cherish her.",
